<text font-family="sans-serif" fill="black" x="230" y="230"
      font-size="16px" font-weight="bold">PC 04.219 Reproducible Radiant Rectangle Classic</text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black" x="230" y="248">Reconstructed by Roland Arajs from top and bottom</text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black" x="230" y="266">views on the internet (url below)</text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black" x="230" y="284">Orignal design was by Henry Grossbard</text>
<text font-family="sans-serif" font-size="14px" fill="black"><tspan x="230" y="302">Angles for R.I. = 1.540</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="320">61 facets + 8 girdles</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="338">2-fold, mirror-image symmetry; 96 index</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="356">L/W = 1.334  T/W = 0.869  U/W = 0.579</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="374">P/W = 0.756 C/W = 0.138</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="392">Vol/W&#179; = 0.564</tspan>
<tspan x="230" y="410">pc04219.asc</tspan>
